      en: "Lenggong Valley in Perak is a significant archaeological site and UNESCO World Heritage Site. It contains evidence of human habitation dating back up to 1.83 million years, including the oldest stone tools found outside Africa. The valley encompasses several caves and open-air sites that have revealed tools from the Paleolithic and Neolithic periods. The discovery of the 'Perak Man', a 10,000-year-old human skeleton, is among the most notable finds. The site was inscribed as a UNESCO site in 2012. Lenggong Valley provides insights into early human migration and adaptation in Southeast Asia.",
