      en: "Kundasang War Memorial in Sabah commemorates Australian and British soldiers who died during the Sandakan Death March in World War II. Erected in 1962, it is located on a hill overlooking Mount Kinabalu. The memorial features four pavilions representing the different nations involved. It recalls the approximately 2,400 prisoners who perished. The site is a place of reflection and an important historical monument. It is maintained by Sabah Tourism Board and honored annually by many visitors.",
