      en: "Pasir Salak Historical Complex in Perak is a memorial for Malay national hero Datuk Maharaja Lela. It is the site where British resident J.W.W. Birch was assassinated in 1877. The complex includes a museum, a mausoleum, and a monument. Located on the banks of the Perak River, it commemorates resistance against British colonial rule. Opened in 1995, it is an important historical center. The complex provides insights into Malay history and the struggle for independence.",
