      en: "The Chimney on Labuan is a 32-meter tall brick chimney dating from the 19th century. It was completed in 1909 and was part of the coal mining operations of the Labuan Coal Company. The chimney is the only remaining structure of the industrial complex. It stands on a hill near Tanjung Kubong. The purpose of the chimney is disputed – either for ventilation or smoke exhaust. It was renovated in 1989. Today it is a tourist attraction and listed as a national heritage.",
