      en: "The Petagas War Memorial in Kota Kinabalu, Sabah, Malaysia, commemorates the victims of the Japanese occupation of Borneo (1942–1945). It was erected in 1952 and stands at the site of the execution of about 300 civilians and guerrillas by the Japanese on 21 January 1944. The memorial consists of a white cross and commemorative plaques. Surrounded by trees, it is a place of reflection. Annual remembrance services are held. The memorial is maintained by the local government.",
